IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `plan55-nouns`
IMPORT `plan55-cross-references`

-- Row il-55. EXPECTED RED: six assertions, all failing. The count (6) is declared in check.sh and in encoding.json.
-- Each states what the citing words need: a target that is what they say it is, and, for the repealed section, a text that is in force on a day long after the repeal.
-- Defect A: section 145ב(ב)(7)(א) cites "145(א2)(4)" and "145(א3)(4)". The consolidation prints (א2) as one sentence with no paragraph (4), and prints paragraph (4) of (א3) as a rule about an application the engineer did not answer,
-- while the citing words describe the Minister's setting of preconditions, which the consolidation prints in paragraph (2) of (א3). So both fail. Limb (a) is the consolidation only; limb (b) is the page image of Sefer HaChukim 2450 p. 510.
-- Defect B: regulation 83(א) cites "257א". The official text says that section 257א was repealed (Sefer HaChukim 2635 p. 920, section 6; in force six months after 25 April 2017, p. 923, section 16(א)),
-- so both fail. Limb (b) is read from the page image of Kovetz HaTakanot 7682 p. 1535.
-- Defect C: the definition of "respondent" cites "198א", and the consolidation prints no such section. It fails on the words as printed; reading B (198(א)) passes and is in plan55-tests-xrefs.l4 as a record of that reading.
-- Defect D: regulation 2(ד) cites "202(ה)(2)", and the consolidation prints section 202 with no subsections. It fails on the number as printed; reading B (202ה(2)) passes and is in plan55-tests-xrefs.l4 as a record of that reading.
-- Nothing here is edited to make it pass.

§ `Defect A: the citing words cite places that are not what they describe`

-- 1. The first citation: the description of the target is not the description of what the citing words point at.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), first citation, to s 145(א2)(4)`)
-- 2. The second citation: the same.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 145ב(ב)(7)(א), second citation, to s 145(א3)(4)`)

§ `Defect B: the citing words name a section that is not there`

-- 3. The description of the target is not the description of what the citing words point at.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: reg 83(א) of the licensing regulations to s 257א`)
-- 4. The text the citing words name is not in force on a day long after the repeal.
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: reg 83(א) of the licensing regulations to s 257א`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Defect C: the citing words cite a section the consolidation does not have`

-- 5. The description of the target is not the description of what the citing words point at.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: respondent definition, as printed, to s 198א`)

§ `Defect D: the citing words cite a subsection the consolidation does not have`

-- 6. The description of the target is not the description of what the citing words point at.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: reg 2(ד) of the pay regulations, as printed, to s 202(ה)(2)`)
